From 3daa2f24cef26d54e0d2cfe5671f37dd2d6f855a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:52:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] port 09aedda6 324b1d80: conversation cache: a request
 that starts with a shallow checkpoint of a parked conversation borrows it on
 a layer split too, the image goes back to its place (opt-in
 STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1, #1164)

Rebuilt as an extension of upstream's borrow (c9e571e0: ConversationCache::borrows / guard, restore_prefix),
which is gated on stages.empty() and so never runs on a layer split.  09aedda6 + its fixup 324b1d80 squashed.

Adaptations:
- borrows(m, shallow): STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1 adds our rule 2 * match < the entry's live length to upstream's
  (not live, below the deepest checkpoint, no pin at or below; the serial check is upstream's).  It applies on one
  GPU too, where the borrow itself stays upstream's (donor stays parked, guarded, restore_prefix).  Our own
  conversation_borrow_rule is dropped: upstream's borrows() is the rule.
- the split path (borrow_whole, STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1 and stages non-empty): the entry is taken as before (the
  outgoing park counts it as held - also park_capture_take's held for an in-flight STRATA_PARK_CAPTURE - and can
  neither evict nor supersede it), validated and restored whole, then the borrower copies the checkpoints at or
  below its resume point with their stage parts (conversation_borrow_checkpoints, as ours), skips retain(), and
  put_back(image, serial) returns it.  The copy runs before the branch; a failure takes the image (324b1d80).
- put_back takes the Match's serial: v0.2.12 keeps entry identities in serials_ (not a park_serial field in the
  image as ours did), so SavedConversation is unchanged; the supersede check swaps serials_ and guarded_ too, and
  the insert keeps serials_ in ascending order.
- never from the SSD tier (from_tier).  The STRATA_READ_YIELD exclusion (yield_pin < 0) is not in this branch yet
  (READ_YIELD is P9) and must be added there.
- the split borrow also counts in upstream's borrowed() (count_borrow) and logs borrowed=N after checkpoints=.
- the "restored" line names the donor's length only with the switch on ("restored N of M tokens"), and
  "(borrow failed (copy), taken)" after a failed copy; off: byte-identical to v0.2.12.
- conversation_cache_test: the shallow rule through the cache (incl. the production 8192 / 132245 of 132362
  cases), put_back's LRU place, accounting, slot count, budget, supersede and pinned-only cases, and the checkpoint
  copy with and without a layer split, adapted to serials.

Off (STRATA_PARK_BORROW unset): borrows(m, false) is upstream's, borrow_whole is false, the take path and its log
line are v0.2.12's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
